// A dotted half in VOICE THREE against eighths in voice two (起票 2026-08-05,
// scratch/ベースタブLy/Untitled-4.lys, reproduced verbatim). Two LilyPond mechanisms meet
// on the first eighth gap, and both were mis-ported:
//   ① the third voice's collision shift is automatic_shift's `Stem::is_valid_stem ?
//     … : offset += 0.5` clause × the down head — MEASURED on 2.26.0: cis' sits
//     +0.652 right of the column. Lily#'s old hand-rolled cascade put it at +1.3042
//     (a flat +1 head width for every later same-direction voice), twice LilyPond's.
//   ② the shifted cis2. reaches its DOT into the next eighth column, which belongs to
//     voice two alone; the spring's minimum is the columns' skyline distance over the
//     staff's separation boxes (note-spacing.cc:78-83), which carry the shifts. The
//     old per-voice-only rod loop never formed the cis→d pair, so the dot printed
//     straight THROUGH the d's head (same X band, same Y row —
//     SpacingRules.ApplyCrossVoiceColumnSpacing holds the derivation).
// MEASURED (2.26.0 twin): first eighth gap 3.33 vs the measure's plain 2.50 — and
// with the dot removed (cis2 for cis2.) it collapses back to 2.51 even though the
// shifted head stays, so the push is the dot's skyline, not the head's.
part melody {
  section A { voice { g''2( g8) eis fis g } { e8 d e e e fis r4 }  { cis2. r4 } }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff melody
}
